The voting rights act was a decisive blow against Jim Crow and the forces of white supremacy that propped it up. Latino, black, Asian, and other communities have built political representation and power for decades because of this landmark legislation. And that's why Republicans have spent decades trying to gut the voting rights act. They don't redraw maps because we're weak, they redraw maps, because we're powerful. They fear black power. They fear Latino power. They fear Asian power. They fear the power of people of all races and ethnicities standing together and saying, we will not bow to white supremacy.
